{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 38, :comments ["<b>ויצג.</b> Its Targum is וְדָעִיץ — it is an Aramaic term of thrusting and driving in. And many instances are in the Talmud: דָּצָהּ וּשְׁלָפָהּ, דַּץ בֵּיהּ מִידֵי, דָּצָהּ — like דְעָצָהּ, except that it shortens the word." "<b>ברהטים.</b> In the water channels — in the troughs made in the ground to water the flocks there." "<b>אשר תבאן וגו'.</b> In the water channels where the flocks would come to drink there — there he set the rods opposite the flock." "<b>ויחמנה.</b> The animal sees the rods and recoils backward, and the male mounts her and she gives birth accordingly. Rabbi Hoshaya says: the waters became seed in their wombs and they had no need of a male — and this is ״וַיֵּחַמְנָה וגו׳״ (Bereshit Rabbah)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:01:23.090179917Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}